---
import Layout from '../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Lesson 11: Robot Arm Stage 1 (Base + Elbow) - C00lnerd Tutoring">
    <div style="max-width: 1000px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 2rem;">
        
        <!-- Header -->
        <div style="background: linear-gradient(135deg, #667eea 0%, #764ba2 100%); color: white; padding: 3rem; border-radius: 15px; margin-bottom: 2rem; text-align: center;">
            <h1 style="font-size: 2.5rem; font-weight: bold; margin: 0 0 1rem 0;">Lesson 11: Robot Arm Stage 1 (Base + Elbow)</h1>
            <p style="font-size: 1.2rem; margin: 0 0 1rem 0; opacity: 0.9;">Start a recurring build thread with SG90 servos</p>
            <div style="background: rgba(255,255,255,0.1); padding: 1rem; border-radius: 8px; margin-top: 1.5rem;">
                <p style="margin: 0; font-weight: 600;">🦾 This semester’s main hands-on project: build a robot arm one stage at a time</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Learning Objectives -->
        <div style="background: white; padding: 2rem; border-radius: 15px; box-shadow: 0 4px 6px rgba(0,0,0,0.1); margin-bottom: 2rem;">
            <h2 style="color: #667eea; font-size: 1.8rem; font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">🎯 Learning Objectives</h2>
            
            <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 2rem;">
                <div>
                    <h3 style="color: #2d3748; font-size: 1.3rem; font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 1rem;">Stage 1 Goals:</h3>
                    <ul style="list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0; color: #4a5568; line-height: 1.8;">
                        <li>• Control two SG90 servos as a base + elbow</li>
                        <li>• Use a consistent pin map that we’ll reuse in future lessons</li>
                        <li>• Create a safe “joint tester” program (manual + sweep test)</li>
                        <li>• Prepare for mounting the servos into 3D printed parts</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <h3 style="color: #2d3748; font-size: 1.3rem; font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 1rem;">Skills Developed:</h3>
                    <ul style="list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0; color: #4a5568; line-height: 1.8;">
                        <li>• Servo wiring and power planning</li>
                        <li>• Input-to-output control (read → decide → act)</li>
                        <li>• Testing, calibration, and safe limits</li>
                        <li>• Building larger projects in stages</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Section 1: Parts Inventory -->
        <div style="background: white; padding: 2rem; border-radius: 15px; box-shadow: 0 4px 6px rgba(0,0,0,0.1); margin-bottom: 2rem;">
            <h2 style="color: #667eea; font-size: 1.8rem; font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">📦 Section 1: Parts Inventory</h2>
            
            <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 2rem;">
                <div style="background: #e6fffa; padding: 1.5rem; border-radius: 8px;">
                    <h4 style="color: #2d3748; font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 1rem;">Electronic Components:</h4>
                    <ul style="list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0; color: #4a5568; line-height: 1.8;">
                        <li>• Arduino Uno microcontroller</li>
                        <li>• 2x SG90 micro servos (base + elbow)</li>
                        <li>• Breadboard (or expansion board) + jumper wires</li>
                        <li>• Push button (A2 to GND, INPUT_PULLUP)</li>
                        <li>• Potentiometer (A0) for angle control</li>
                        <li>• Buzzer (optional) for mode-change feedback</li>
                        <li>• Jumper wires and connectors</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
                <div style="background: #fff7ed; padding: 1.5rem; border-radius: 8px;">
                    <h4 style="color: #2d3748; font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 1rem;">Mechanical Parts:</h4>
                    <ul style="list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0; color: #4a5568; line-height: 1.8;">
                        <li>• (Optional) 3D printed base mount</li>
                        <li>• (Optional) 3D printed elbow bracket</li>
                        <li>• Small screws (servo horn screws + mounting hardware)</li>
                        <li>• Zip ties or tape for temporary mounting (prototype stage)</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div style="background: #f0f9ff; padding: 1.5rem; border-radius: 8px; margin-top: 1.5rem;">
                <h4 style="color: #2d3748; font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 1rem;">🔧 Required Tools:</h4>
                <ul style="list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0; color: #4a5568; line-height: 1.8;">
                    <li>• Phillips head screwdriver</li>
                    <li>• Small pliers</li>
                    <li>• Wire strippers (if needed)</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Robot Arm Build Thread -->
        <div style="background: white; padding: 2rem; border-radius: 15px; box-shadow: 0 4px 6px rgba(0,0,0,0.1); margin-bottom: 2rem;">
            <h2 style="color: #667eea; font-size: 1.8rem; font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">🧵 Robot Arm Build Thread</h2>
            
            <div style="background: #f0f9ff; padding: 1.5rem; border-radius: 8px; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">
                <h4 style="color: #2d3748; font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 1rem;">Standard Pin Map (keep this consistent)</h4>
                <ul style="margin: 0; padding-left: 1.25rem; color: #4a5568; line-height: 1.8;">
                    <li><strong>Button:</strong> A2 (to GND, INPUT_PULLUP)</li>
                    <li><strong>Potentiometer:</strong> A0</li>
                    <li><strong>Buzzer (optional):</strong> pin 8</li>
                    <li><strong>Base servo signal:</strong> pin 9</li>
                    <li><strong>Elbow servo signal:</strong> pin 10</li>
                </ul>
            </div>

            <div style="background: #e6fffa; padding: 1.5rem; border-radius: 8px;">
                <h4 style="color: #2d3748; font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 1rem;">Progress Checklist</h4>
                <ul style="list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0; color: #4a5568; line-height: 1.8;">
                    <li>☐ Base servo responds reliably (manual control)</li>
                    <li>☐ Elbow servo responds reliably (manual control)</li>
                    <li>☐ Both servos can run a safe sweep test without jittering</li>
                    <li>☐ Safe limits are enforced (example: 20°–160°)</li>
                    <li>☐ (Optional) Buzzer cue plays when you change modes</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Wiring and Connections -->
        <div style="background: white; padding: 2rem; border-radius: 15px; box-shadow: 0 4px 6px rgba(0,0,0,0.1); margin-bottom: 2rem;">
            <h2 style="color: #667eea; font-size: 1.8rem; font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">🔌 Wiring and Connections</h2>
            
            <div style="background: #fef2f2; padding: 1.5rem; border-radius: 8px; margin-bottom: 1.5rem; border-left: 4px solid #dc2626;">
                <h4 style="color: #dc2626; font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">⚠️ Safety First!</h4>
                <p style="color: #4a5568; margin: 0; line-height: 1.6;">
                    Always disconnect power before making any connections. SG90 servos can draw bursts of current. If a servo jitters or resets your Arduino,
                    consider powering the servos from a separate 5V source (and connect grounds).
                </p>
            </div>

            <div style="margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">
                <h3 style="color: #2d3748; font-size: 1.3rem; font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 1rem;">Power Connections</h3>
                <div style="background: #e6fffa; padding: 1.5rem; border-radius: 8px;">
                    <ul style="list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0; color: #4a5568; line-height: 1.8;">
                        <li>• Start with a single servo powered from Arduino 5V (test)</li>
                        <li>• If the Arduino resets or the servo jitters, use an external 5V supply for servos</li>
                        <li>• Always connect all grounds together (Arduino GND ↔ servo power supply GND)</li>
                        <li>• Verify voltage levels before powering on</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div style="margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">
                <h3 style="color: #2d3748; font-size: 1.3rem; font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 1rem;">Signal Connections</h3>
                <div style="background: #f0f9ff; padding: 1.5rem; border-radius: 8px;">
                    <ul style="list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0; color: #4a5568; line-height: 1.8;">
                        <li>• Base servo signal → pin 9</li>
                        <li>• Elbow servo signal → pin 10</li>
                        <li>• Button → A2 to GND (INPUT_PULLUP)</li>
                        <li>• Potentiometer wiper → A0 (other pins to 5V and GND)</li>
                        <li>• (Optional) Buzzer → pin 8 to GND</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Testing and Troubleshooting -->
        <div style="background: white; padding: 2rem; border-radius: 15px; box-shadow: 0 4px 6px rgba(0,0,0,0.1); margin-bottom: 2rem;">
            <h2 style="color: #667eea; font-size: 1.8rem; font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">🧪 Testing and Troubleshooting</h2>
            
            <div style="margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">
                <h3 style="color: #2d3748; font-size: 1.3rem; font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 1rem;">Initial Testing Checklist</h3>
                <div style="background: #e6fffa; padding: 1.5rem; border-radius: 8px;">
                    <ul style="list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0; color: #4a5568; line-height: 1.8;">
                        <li>✅ Visual inspection of all servo wires (signal/power/ground)</li>
                        <li>✅ Test each servo individually with the Lesson 10 “basic servo control” sketch</li>
                        <li>✅ Confirm button and potentiometer read correctly</li>
                        <li>✅ Add safe limits before attaching any printed parts</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div style="margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">
                <h3 style="color: #2d3748; font-size: 1.3rem; font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 1rem;">Common Issues and Solutions</h3>
                <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 1rem;">
                    <div style="background: #fef2f2; padding: 1rem; border-radius: 8px;">
                        <h4 style="color: #dc2626; font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">Problem: Servo jitters</h4>
                        <p style="color: #4a5568; margin: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;">Use a separate 5V supply for servos (shared ground), and avoid long loose jumper wires</p>
                    </div>
                    <div style="background: #fef2f2; padding: 1rem; border-radius: 8px;">
                        <h4 style="color: #dc2626; font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">Problem: Arduino resets when servo moves</h4>
                        <p style="color: #4a5568; margin: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;">The servo is drawing too much current from Arduino 5V—use external 5V for servos</p>
                    </div>
                    <div style="background: #fef2f2; padding: 1rem; border-radius: 8px;">
                        <h4 style="color: #dc2626; font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">Problem: Servo moves in the wrong direction</h4>
                        <p style="color: #4a5568; margin: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;">Reverse the angle mapping in code or re-mount the servo horn after centering at 90°</p>
                    </div>
                    <div style="background: #fef2f2; padding: 1rem; border-radius: 8px;">
                        <h4 style="color: #dc2626; font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">Problem: Servo doesn’t move at all</h4>
                        <p style="color: #4a5568; margin: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;">Check the signal pin number, ensure servo ground is connected, and verify power polarity</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Assessment & Next Steps -->
        <div style="background: white; padding: 2rem; border-radius: 15px; box-shadow: 0 4px 6px rgba(0,0,0,0.1); margin-bottom: 2rem;">
            <h2 style="color: #667eea; font-size: 1.8rem; font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">📝 Assessment & Next Steps</h2>
            
            <div style="margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">
                <h3 style="color: #2d3748; font-size: 1.3rem; font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 1rem;">Stage 1 Verification</h3>
                <div style="background: #f8fafc; padding: 1.5rem; border-radius: 8px;">
                    <p style="color: #4a5568; line-height: 1.6; margin-bottom: 1rem;">
                        Before moving to the next stage, make sure you have a reliable base + elbow setup:
                    </p>
                    <ul style="list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0; color: #4a5568; line-height: 1.8;">
                        <li>� Button + potentiometer inputs work reliably</li>
                        <li>🦾 Both servos respond correctly and smoothly</li>
                        <li>⚡ Power is stable (no resets during movement)</li>
                        <li>�️ Safe limits are enabled before you attach printed parts</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div style="background: #e6fffa; padding: 1.5rem; border-radius: 8px; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">
                <h4 style="color: #2d3748; font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 1rem;">🎯 Preparation for Week 12</h4>
                <p style="color: #4a5568; line-height: 1.6; margin: 0;">
                    Next, we’ll expand the arm by adding a <strong>shoulder joint</strong> and introduce “preset poses” (home, ready, reach) so the arm can move through repeatable sequences.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div style="text-center">
                <a href="/programming/quizzes32/lesson11" style="background-color: #7c3aed; color: white; padding: 12px 24px; border-radius: 8px; text-decoration: none; font-weight: 600; border: 2px solid #6d28d9; box-shadow: 0 4px 6px -1px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1); transition: all 0.2s; display: inline-block;" onmouseover="this.style.backgroundColor='#6d28d9'; this.style.transform='translateY(-2px)'; this.style.boxShadow='0 10px 15px -3px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1)'" onmouseout="this.style.backgroundColor='#7c3aed'; this.style.transform='translateY(0px)'; this.style.boxShadow='0 4px 6px -1px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1)'">
                    Take Lesson 11 Quiz →
                </a>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Navigation -->
        <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; margin-top: 2rem;">
            <div>
                <a href="/programming/lessons32/lesson10" style="background-color: #6b7280; color: white; padding: 12px 20px; border-radius: 8px; text-decoration: none; font-weight: 600; border: 2px solid #4b5563; box-shadow: 0 4px 6px -1px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1); transition: all 0.2s; display: inline-block;" onmouseover="this.style.backgroundColor='#4b5563'; this.style.transform='translateY(-2px)'; this.style.boxShadow='0 10px 15px -3px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1)'" onmouseout="this.style.backgroundColor='#6b7280'; this.style.transform='translateY(0px)'; this.style.boxShadow='0 4px 6px -1px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1)'">
                    ← Previous: Lesson 10
                </a>
            </div>
            <div>
                <a href="/programming/" style="background-color: #059669; color: white; padding: 12px 20px; border-radius: 8px; text-decoration: none; font-weight: 600; border: 2px solid #047857; box-shadow: 0 4px 6px -1px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1); transition: all 0.2s; display: inline-block;" onmouseover="this.style.backgroundColor='#047857'; this.style.transform='translateY(-2px)'; this.style.boxShadow='0 10px 15px -3px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1)'" onmouseout="this.style.backgroundColor='#059669'; this.style.transform='translateY(0px)'; this.style.boxShadow='0 4px 6px -1px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1)'">
                    Course Overview
                </a>
            </div>
            <div>
                <a href="/programming/lessons32/lesson12" style="background-color: #2563eb; color: white; padding: 12px 20px; border-radius: 8px; text-decoration: none; font-weight: 600; border: 2px solid #1d4ed8; box-shadow: 0 4px 6px -1px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1); transition: all 0.2s; display: inline-block;" onmouseover="this.style.backgroundColor='#1d4ed8'; this.style.transform='translateY(-2px)'; this.style.boxShadow='0 10px 15px -3px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1)'" onmouseout="this.style.backgroundColor='#2563eb'; this.style.transform='translateY(0px)'; this.style.boxShadow='0 4px 6px -1px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1)'">
                    Next: Lesson 12 →
                </a>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</Layout>
